    "oldRow": "| Leave/cleanup |0044b090's all-five-owner test and0044b070 draw/scroll behavior are retained. Owner identities: HUD0098db0c, object0098db48, cell0098db44, status0098db2c from00504bc0, message0098db40 from004314c0. | Bind owner reset/retention lifecycle, including indirect paths, before universal leave/re-entry behavior. The bounded dispatcher does not prove universal clear or retention. This is a specific five-word producer/reset closure, not permission for a broad UI inventory. |",
    "newRow": "| Leave/cleanup |0044b090 tests HUD0098db0c, object0098db48, cell0098db44, status0098db2c and message0098db40. Object/cell helpers clear and repopulate only their own words when invoked. The ordinary no-handler return leaves owners unchanged;0044b070 only changes scroll fields, so any retained nonzero word prevents cleanup. Neighboring indirect writes are bounded away. | Native ordinary retention is proved (A). Implement caller-conditioned no-handler retention, blank-cell/unnamed-object category transitions, all-five-zero cleanup and independent forced/explicit resets. A browser canvas leave does not itself establish which native owner branch occurred; preserve actual HUD/cell history and renderer draw ownership. |",
    "scope": "Only Leave/cleanup row; no other native area reopened."
  },
